==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|attractive|-ness}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The state of being [[attractive]] or [[engaging]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1999|author=David Weber|title=Echoes of Honor|publisher=Baen Publishing Enterprises|isbn=9781618242006
|passage=Given the vivacious young redhead&#39;s '''attractiveness''', some might have assumed he had more than simply professional reasons for sheepdogging her career, but they would have been wrong. He&#39;d seen something in her&nbsp;...}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=A. J. Oakes|title=Ornamental Grasses and Grasslike Plants|page=462
|passage=The plants are equally attractive when different-colored zebrinas are trained on a fan-shaped or rectangular trellis. The rose-colored flowers, of which new ones blossom each morning, add to the '''attractiveness''' of this viny, succulent herb.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} The result of being [[attractive]].

